Amplifier probe: I2C reads of register 0 at 0x64 (aw2016 LED), 0x58 and 0x5b (aw87xxx).

all11 found I2C firmware with 32-bit FIFOs on SE1. SE1 is set up as the touch driver sets up
SE2 and one byte is read from each chip; the amplifier reset GPIOs are left alone.

--- a/bsd/dev/spes_amp.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/spes_amp.c
@@ -6,7 +6,11 @@
  * firmware and FIFOs on SE1, as the touch driver does for SE2 (bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
  * touch_clocks/touch_se_init): vote the SE1 clock (GCC 0x7900c bit 11, gcc-khaje.c), XO source
  * on its RCG (0x1f278), wait for the branch, then read the SE's firmware and FIFO registers.
- * No bus transfer, no amplifier reset is touched.
+ * With I2C firmware there (all11: proto 3, 32-bit FIFOs) the SE is set up as the touch driver
+ * sets up SE2 and register 0 is read from the aw2016 LED driver at 0x64 (not behind the
+ * amplifier resets: an answer proves the path) and from the amplifiers at 0x58 and 0x5b. The
+ * amplifier reset GPIOs are not touched: without khaje's pin-to-tile table a write could hit
+ * another pin, so a NACK from 0x58/0x5b means they are held in reset.
  */
